{
 "id": "arp-midi",
 "version": "0.1",
 "title": "The arpeggiator on MIDI tracks",
 "category": "Examples",
 "license": "GPL-2.0-or-later",
 "author": "naturarum",
 "description": "EXPERIMENT: emulator-tested only. The ARP key, menu and LED work on MIDI-machine tracks, and a MIDI track whose arp is on plays through the stock arpeggiator: its trigs and live keys feed the arp, and the arp's notes leave on the track's MIDI channel by the path and timing of a stock MIDI trig (N.LEN as the nearest trig length not shorter, INF as one arp period). The trig's MIDI p-locks are not sent while the arp is on. Arp off, the track is stock. With arp-modes, SHUF, RAND and TM play on MIDI tracks too. Our own code, from a study of OS 1.12 (dn2-cfw notes/T2.2-arp-midi-v2.md).",
 "device": "digitone-mk2",
 "os": "1.12",
